\ -15\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-s+t=1 \\\\ 4s-6t=-10 \\\\ 3s-7t=-15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -6 & -10 \\\\ 3 & -7 & -15\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 3 & -7 & -15\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-s+t=1 \\\\ -2t=-6 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-2t=-6\\,⟹\\,t=3.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-s+t & =1 \\\\ -s+3 & =1 \\\\ -s & =-2 \\\\ s & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=2,\\,t=3,$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=2b+3c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=2\\cdot 3=6.$" 13194139534946 true] [17592186321666 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321667 13194139534946 true] [17592186321666 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321668 13194139534946 true] [17592186321666 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321669 13194139534946 true] [17592186321666 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321670 13194139534946 true] [17592186321666 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321671 13194139534946 true] [17592186321666 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534946 true] [17592186321666 1041 "selection" 13194139534946 true] [17592186321666 1104 #edb/ref 17592186321667 13194139534946 true] [17592186321666 1110 #uuid "58a94fa7-ae30-5bc9-8f07-4a3652330594" 13194139534946 true] [17592186321667 1034 "6" 13194139534946 true] [17592186321667 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534946 true] [17592186321667 1111 #uuid "652a9716-b89e-52a2-85ba-011e3168e304" 13